{"missing_check": "Missing installed-state and authentication gate: when phpns is already installed, a visitor must not be able to run install/index.php; only an authenticated user may enter after installation.", "insertion_location": "In install/index.php, between the `define("INSTALLING",1);` statement and the `function db_form(...)` declaration; this is before any `$_GET['step']` dispatch, DB writes, or generated config activities.", "recommended_guard": "@include_once("../inc/config.php");
if (@$globalvars['installed'] == "yes" && @$_SESSION['auth'] != "yes") {
    header("Location: ../login.php");
    die();
}", "reused_project_semantics": "The generated config file (`../inc/config.php`) sets "installed" to "yes" only after a successful install, so `$globalvars['installed']` is the real completion sentinel. `$_SESSION['auth'] == "yes"` is the app's real authenticated-admin sentinel from inc/auth.php, and the redirect+die is its denial style. `@` is used to suppress notices when the config/session value is absent before auth/install.", "reason": "Without this guard, a visitor can reach install/index.php on an already-configured site and drive the installer to overwrite config/database/admin settings. Checking the installed sentinel first blocks this sensitive path for unauthenticated visitors while preserving the fresh-install flow when config.php is absent and preserving the intended admin/authenticated access after installation."}

